# Non-SGML characters (BEL 7, DEL 127) inside the SGML DECLARATION itself
# (reportNonSgmlCharacter over parseSd). onsgmls reads the declaration through
# the same record machinery as the document and reports every non-SGML char it
# tokenizes up to the declaration-closing MDC (`>`) — INCLUDING chars inside
# `--…--` comments and quoted literals; a trailing comment after the MDC is not
# reached. Three positions exercised here:
#   - BEL inside the version literal  (line 1)
#   - BEL inside a comment            (line 3)
#   - DEL as a stray char             (line 184, near APPINFO)
# decl.dcl is a copy of scaly.dcl with those chars injected; the built
# Sd/Syntax is unchanged, so the document parses identically (exit 1, no
# trailing C because the declaration errors are non-conforming). Our scoped
# SdParser has no report path, so parse_to_esis makes a dedicated pass
# (scan_sd_non_sgml) over the declaration's normalized buffer.
BASE=entry
DOC=doc.sgm
